  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: 
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: 'This dish is made from the leftover cuts of blubber
    and fat trimmings from various types of meat. Most cooks put all of these into
    a huge pot, melt it down and reuse it. Irresponsible or lazy cooks might forget
    it and let the fat go rancid. An entrepreneurial cook, however, can still salvage
    this: melt and clarify the fat, pour it into a mold, and let it set before pouring
    the sauce over. Very few could fight off the impulse to spit out this glob of
    fat and salt, but ones that do would find that this shining mass bounces merrily
    all the way down their gullet. '
